---
layout: layouts/page.njk
page_id: search
title: Search
band: standard
eyebrow: ""
heading: Search
summary: Find a sleep problem, a video or a page on this website.
styles: ["pages/search.css"]
scripts: ["search.js"]
# Pages reached from here learn only the site's address, never the query:
# YouTube's player script copies document.referrer into the embed (SPEC §8.1).
referrer: strict-origin
---
{#-
  Search results page (SPEC §8.1). Every search is a plain GET of
  /search/?q=..., from this form or the header's. src/js/search.js reads ?q=,
  loads MiniSearch and the index (the two data- addresses below; menu.js
  prefetches the same files when a header search box gets focus) and fills in
  the status line and the results. The empty and error messages are shown by
  the script; without JavaScript only the fallback shows.
  autocomplete="off", as in the header: typed health terms stay out of the
  browser's form history (the query is still in the address).
-#}
<div class="search-page" data-search data-minisearch="/js/vendor/minisearch/index.js" data-index="/search-index.json">
  <form class="search-form" role="search" action="/search/" method="get" aria-labelledby="search-q-label">
    <label class="search-form__label" id="search-q-label" for="search-q">Search this website</label>
    <div class="search-form__row">
      <input class="search-form__input" id="search-q" name="q" type="search" autocomplete="off" enterkeyhint="search" data-search-input>
      <button class="button button--primary search-form__submit" type="submit">Search</button>
    </div>
  </form>
  {#- Always shown, with or without JavaScript: someone in distress may type it here (SPEC §8.1). #}
  <p class="notice--urgent search-urgent">If you feel unsafe or need help right now, go to <a href="/urgent-help/">Getting urgent help</a>.</p>
  <p class="search-status" role="status" data-search-status></p>
  <ol class="search-results" role="list" data-search-results hidden></ol>
  <div class="search-message" data-search-empty hidden>
    <p>Try other words, or fewer of them. You can also see every topic on the <a href="/problems/">Sleep problems</a> page.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="search-message" data-search-error hidden>
    <p>You can still find every topic on the <a href="/problems/">Sleep problems</a> page.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="search-fallback" data-search-fallback>
    <p>Search results need JavaScript. Without it, you can find every topic on the <a href="/problems/">Sleep problems</a> page.</p>
  </div>
</div>
